# PR Review Workflow

I am a **reviewer** for the [llm-d/llm-d-kv-cache](https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d-kv-cache) project.

## CI & Review Flow (GitHub Actions + Prow-style Commands)

PR CI checks run automatically on `pull_request`:
- **ci-pr-checks**: lint (pre-commit, clang-format), `make build`, `make test`
- **ci-signed-commits**: verify all commits are signed (DCO)
- **ci-examples**: run `hack/verify-examples.sh` (target: main)
- **ci-uds-tokenizer**: UDS tokenizer tests (when relevant paths change)
- **auto-assign**: assigns reviewers from OWNERS file

Prow-style commands (via PR comments, handled by GitHub Actions):
- `/lgtm` — add lgtm label (removed automatically on new commits)
- `/approve` — approve for merge
- `/hold` — prevent auto-merge
- `/rerun` — re-run CI checks
- Both `/lgtm` and `/approve` are needed; `prow-pr-automerge` merges every 5 min

## Triage — When to Skip

- **CI failures**: PRs with failing checks do not need review — skip them.
- **Awaiting reply**: If I have recently commented and no reply yet, **skip**. Inform me it's pending.

## Linking PRs and Issues

Always include the **full URL** — not just `#1234`.

- Good: `[#1234](https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d-kv-cache/pull/1234)`
- Bad: `#1234`

## Comment Style

- **Thank the contributor by name**: e.g. `Thanks @username!`
- **Acknowledge effort**: e.g. "Great work on this!", "Nice improvement!"
- **Thank reviewers/participants too**: Give shout-outs to those who left useful feedback.
- **Be constructive**: Even when requesting changes, pair feedback with appreciation.
